<title>GERMANY: Ministry sees 4.19 mln T German 96/97 sugar output.</title>
<headline>Ministry sees 4.19 mln T German 96/97 sugar output.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's agriculture ministry on Tuesday said sugar production in 1996/97 (October/September) would rise to 4.19 million tonnes whites value after 3.83 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Germany's self-sufficiency rate would be nine points up from the previous campaign at 150 percent.</p>
<p>The ministry said in a weekly circular domestic sugar consumption was estimated at roughly 2.80 million tonnes and 1.40 million tonnes would be available for export.</p>
<p>The higher production result was attributed to the higher sugar content of 18.17 percent (16.73) in the 1996/97 beet campaign.</p>
<p>The beet volume was virtually unchanged from 1995/96 at 26.06 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Yield and area figures were also little changed.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
